Z||000006||four50four||12-29-1999||04:18 PM||||dennis lagura is in the process of doing a 3.4 turbo. he's aiming for 300 hp. here's his page on turbocharging the stock 2.8...  <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/dlagrua/turbo.htm</A> . I emailed him a while ago and he said it SHOULD be complete in January.||||reg||6
Z||000007||WKDFIRO||12-30-1999||12:05 AM||||There is a air to water intercooled, water injected, 3.4 turbo automatic in existance. The biggest problem was to fabricate the headers so that they wouldn't crack. The stock manifolds just wont take it. Wishing that I had a scanner for a pic! Fiero Motorsports built it and has been tweaking it on again and off again for a while depending on what kind itch the owner gets. We haven't gotten numbers on it since the 3.4 went in but I am now convinced that the best turbos are automatics! Since the rpms dont diminish when shifting you have nonstop charge! WHOOOOSHHHHHHH!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||87PegasusGT||01-03-2000||04:59 PM||||Regarding the Intercooler setup, I was going to go with the one made by ACE on the Series II. Does anyone have any feedback on this?<BR>Also; anyone besides ACE make an installation kit for the 3800sc? ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||01-03-2000||05:34 PM||||I'm most likely going to get pounded on this but if you are running a Series II S/C, I really don't think you need an intercooler. With a modified pulley and wastegate power is not much of a problem. I haven't checked with ACE but I would imagine that it would be a water to air style  intercooler and that won't be  cheap. Also you would have to modify your trunk lid. The $$ could be used in a much more productive manner.<BR>My S/C 3800 goes like a scalded cat now and I'm afraid that with more power my trunk lid would be automaticly modified by Getrag. I'm running with Vettes now, I really don't need to run with Vipers (but I sure did scare one). <BR>Boy I'm on a roll now, but I think that a good analogy is the exhaust porting deal vs. headers. The home porting job gives about 8 HP(dyno checked) 0$- headers give 9-10 HP 500$  doesn't take a rocket scientist to figure that one out. Anybody know what the intercooler adds(not guesstimates)?||||reg||1
Z||000011||2birds||01-03-2000||10:16 PM||||Hey, Phil, eat a 'Vette for me, too.<P>As far as what an intercooler is worth, My Seat o' the Pants meter tells me that my T-bird SC pulled a LOT harder than a Grand Prix GTP.  The birds used an M-90 blower, and my 94 had the higher flow casing. ||||reg||1
